Date: 10 FEB 1980 2018-EST
From: H at MIT-AI (Jack Holloway)
Subject: Yield testing of 2nd batch of bonded parts
To: (BUG SCHIP) at MIT-AI

We have made a preliminary pass over the overglassed
chips, with the following results:

Chip #		Comment
------		-------
6		Won, runs at PHI1=1500, PHI2=250
7		Won, 1500, 500 ?
8		Lose, fails at State 277, apparently to-address-VAL doesn't work ?
9		Lose, won't even Freeze state
10		Lose, Nano sequencing fails
11		Won, 2000, 625 (or better)
12		Won, 2000, 625   "
13		Lose, (Dropped on floor)
14		Lose, load state to 657
15		Lose, Nano problem
16		Lose, Bus always 77717777 ?
17		Lose, Nano problem
18		Lose, State loads to 676, not 776
19		Lose, State loads to 756, not 776
20		Lose, State 437 always ???
21		Lose, dies between 0-400 steps ??
22		Lose, state always 0
23		Lose, state always 0
24		Won, 2000,625
25		Lose, Bus always all ones

This indicates a 25% yield in the second batch of chips.
The chips tested at PHI1=2000ns, PHI2=625 were not tried at
a higher speed.  Chip 7, however, seems to need a longer PHI2
than 250ns, but we haven't really examined the failure carefully.


