Date: 4 DEC 1979 0143-EST
From: h at MIT-AI (Jack Holloway)
Sent-by: CARL0 at MIT-AI
Subject: Simulation of interpreter
To: (BUG SCHIP) at MIT-AI

After 907 half-steps, the losing chip managed to run
a user program to completion!
   (BLOCK
    (ASET' H (LAMBDA (X)
	       (LAMBDA (Y Z) (CONS (CONS Y X) Z))))
    ((H 1) H 3))

   which produced:
   ((1 . #<closure 21>) . 3)

This has checked out a good part of the S-code ops,
but many primitives like rplacx, eq, cond, peano's, etc.
weren't tested.  Also, the garbage collector has been
simulated in several non-working forms, and we are trusting
that the last bug fix was the final one.  In addition, interrupts
and GC-NEEDED hasn't really been checked.

But we can probably go ahead and fry some silicon, the chip
will likely generate and collect garbage, which is all
it is good for anyway.

