From: H at MIT-AI (Jack Holloway)
Subject: The fix for the TYPE-EQ-BUS testing the mark bit
To: (BUG SCHIP) at MIT-AI

Alan:

To fix the bug where the VAL register tests the mark bit
as part of the type, the cell
	(THE COLUMN-3 REGISTER-ARRAY REGISTERS-WITH-DRIVERS COMPLETE-REGISTERS SCHIP2)
needs to be edited so that one of the 8 TYPE-FIELD-ROWS called is a new
version that has an HEQ-DUMMY in place of the HEQ.

The following CIF defined in 2.5 micron lambdas is the new symbol and
the corrected version of COLUMN-3.


DS 1200;     ( Name: TYPE-FIELD-ROW-NO-HEQ );
( 21 Items. );
(A new symbol almost like 1020);
C 1019 T 142500,0;
C 1017 T 133000,0;
C 1017 T 123500,0;
C 1017 T 114000,0;
C 1017 T 104500,0;
C 1017 T 95000,0;
C 1018 T 93000,0;
C 1017 T 83500,0;
C 1014 T 82000,0;
C 1009 T 70750,0; (was C 1013 T 70750,0);
C 1006 T 60750,0;
C 1008 T 59500,0;
C 1007 T 48750,0;
C 1009 T 37500,0;
C 1006 T 27500,0;
C 1008 T 26250,0;
C 1007 T 15500,0;
C 1006 T 5500,0;
C 1002 T 3750,0;
C 1001 T 1250,0;
C 1000;
DF;


DS 1021;     ( Name: COLUMN-3 );
( 8 Items. );
C 1020 T 0,70000;
C 1020 T 0,60000;
C 1020 T 0,50000;
